{
  "dom_id": "step-q132294",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Using the normal approximation to the binomial distribution, approximate the probability that a soccer player scores $16$ out of $25$ penalties if the player has a $58%$ probability of scoring each penalty. Give your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n*Hint: The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6554\\,$ | $\\,0.6591\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7257\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "Given a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ if \n\n- $np>5,$ and\n\n- $n(1-p)>5,$\n\nwe can approximate $X$ as a normal random variable $Y$ with mean $\\mu =np$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p),$ that is, \n\n$$\nY∼N(np,np(1-p)).\n$$\n\nHere, we have $n=25$ and $p=0.58.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}np & =25\\cdot 0.58 \\\\  & =14.5 \\\\  & >5\\,✓ \\\\ n(1-p) & =25\\cdot (1-0.58) \\\\  & =10.5 \\\\  & >5.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can approximate our binomial random variable $X$ with a normal random variable $Y$ with mean\n\n$$\n\\mu =np=(25)(0.58)=14.5\n$$\n\nand variance\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=np(1-p)=(25)(0.58)(1-0.58)=6.09.\n$$\n\nThat is, we can approximate $X$ by $Y∼N(14.5,6.09).$\n\nNow, we can approximate the desired probability $P(X=16).$ Using a continuity correction, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=16)≈P(15.5\\le Y\\le 16.5).\n$$\n\nTo compute this probability, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(15.5\\le Y\\le 16.5) & =P(\\frac{15.5-14.5}{\\sqrt{6.09}}\\le Z\\le \\frac{16.5-14.5}{\\sqrt{6.09}}) \\\\  & ≈P(0.41\\le Z\\le 0.81) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.81)-P(Z<0.41) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.81)-P(Z\\le 0.41) \\\\  & =Φ(0.81)-Φ(0.41) \\\\  & =0.7910-0.6591 \\\\  & =0.132\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=16)≈0.132.\n$$\n\nNote: Using a software package for the approximation gives a probability of $0.1363.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
